WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.100
Welcome to Managing Performance and Measurement. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Measure what matters and use the results to improve performance.

2
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:20.350
Consider this scenario. A team reports twenty metrics but makes no decisions. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:30.940
Start with two steps: Define measurable business outcomes. Then Specify measures and collection rules. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:40.660
Continue with Analyze variation and trends. Then Change course and check effects. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:40.660 --> 00:01:00.370
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous metric dictionary, baseline results, decision log tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: confusing a large dashboard with performance management; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:14.620
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
